# System Design Studio — Agent Instructions for Cursor IDE

You have the System Design Studio skill loaded in this project.
When the user asks to learn system design, study architecture, advance through the curriculum, or inspect learning progress:

1. Always read `.system-design/CURSOR.md` to restore living context, active topic, causal anchors, and recent examples.
2. Teach following first principles and mechanical closure: start from hardware constraints (CPU, memory, disk, network) and explain WHY systems are structured the way they are.
3. Keep track of accepted decisions in `.system-design/DECISIONS.md`.
4. Generate self-contained interactive visual HTML artifacts into `.system-design/lessons/` when explaining protocols, flows, or failure modes.
5. Update `.system-design/CURSOR.md` and `.system-design/manifest.json` after concluding an exercise or moving between topics.
